                 antcn_lo - Use antcn to configure local LOs

  Syntax:     antcn_lo

  Response:   none

Settable parameters: none

Monitor-only Parameters: none

Comments:

This command is a no-op unless the environment variable FS_ANTCN_LO_MODE is
set. That variable provides the local 'antcn' mode (greater than 99) that will
be triggered to configure the LOs based on the settings in shared memory.

This command is intended to provided a way to implement configuring the LOs
without having to write a local SNAP command. It can be used in the
'ifd_local' procedure, usually found the 'station' SNAP procedure library. As
of FS 10.3, 'drudg' inserts a call to 'ifd_local' at the end of IF setup
procedure ('ifdXX') for each mode.
